WEBVTT

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.660
So as of today, we're second-years.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.410
It makes me nervous to think
we have underclassmen.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.030
Yeah.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:32.360
What's he doing?

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.370
Yamajirou...
What's he doing?

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:35.660
Yamajirou...

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.630
Yamada the Masked Upperclassman I...

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:40.580
Hey!

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:45.560
He's writing down names he wants
his underclassmen to call him!

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.560
Man, this is majorly creepy. Way too weird.
No! Don't look!

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:52.770
Well, they're gonna give us names
like this eventually, right?

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:56.100
So why not start giving it some thought now?

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.450
<i>Delusional weirdo.</i>

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:59.610
Like, Amami would be...

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:01.600
The Medium.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.170
Inoue would be...

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.320
Miss Difficult, maybe!

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.000
Hey! What does that mean?!

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.480
You <i>do</i> have a point.

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:12.380
Right?

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.970
I'm glad you understand, Messiah.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:18.470
Okay, why don't we step outside?

00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:01.530
I want to help the new first-years as best I can!

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.310
You sound pretty enthusiastic.

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:06.320
You think you can handle it?

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:08.040
Yes!

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:13.880
<i>I think the bigger question would be...</i>

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.590
<i>...if the new students are even gonna accept her?</i>

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.180
Good morning.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:27.230
Oh, Amami, good morning.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:29.180
Good morning.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.440
Something's in there!

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:36.940
Wait!

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:41.440
This is the reference room.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:43.540
Thank you ver—

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:49.370
They said to put the materials over there...

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.500
I'm exhausted from gym class.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.040
Yeah.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:53.620
Excuse me!

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:56.840
Your braid's coming loose. Shall I fix it?

00:03:57.820 --> 00:03:59.340
Thank you, Amami.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:03.390
<i>Huh?</i>

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:07.010
<i>There's only one of her, and two braids...</i>

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:07.850
<i>Huh?!</i>

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:08.840
And then—

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:17.670
I'm scared!

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:31.700
Did I scare all those first-years?

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:34.310
Amami's really down.

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:36.610
Well, they were all pretty terrified.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:37.960
Hmph. So what?

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:42.340
<i>So she scared some kids she doesn't
even know. Why get so upset?</i>

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:44.230
Uh-oh.

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:46.850
Miss Difficult's getting jealous.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:48.870
Who are you calling Miss Difficult?!

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.350
I know!

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.850
Let's give her a new image!

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:54.440
A new image?

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:55.500
Yes.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:58.690
Before your "scary girl" image
completely takes hold,

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:01.570
we'll show them that you're not scary at all!

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:04.900
For you, Yamada, that's not a bad idea.

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:06.820
Yeah, that might be...

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:09.840
Hey, it's Doofus Yamada!

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.660
So this is Doofus Yamada's class.

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:14.090
See?

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:16.540
Looks like his doofus image
has taken hold already.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:19.420
L-Let's give her a new image...

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.870
Hey, not bad.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:27.320
You kinda look more spunky that way.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.530
Y-You think so?

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:32.180
Yes.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.600
Please, anything but that.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.420
That looks pretty mature.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:44.630
Y-You think so?

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:46.200
Wanna try blogging, too?

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:46.860
Okay!

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:59.740
All right!

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:06.260
Bring on the fight!

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:07.470
You can drop that!

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:15.480
Now what's <i>that</i> supposed to be?!

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:20.480
I-It's not like I'm happy about this or anything.

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:22.860
What <i>is</i> this?!

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:27.110
W-Well, I'm off.

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:29.200
Good luck!

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:31.990
Just a thought,

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:35.930
but isn't it the ghosts that make
everyone scared of Amami?

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:36.850
Yeah.

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:42.470
Then changing her image won't do her any—

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:44.790
It didn't work...

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:49.880
<i>I figured.</i>

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.230
There, there.

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:55.390
I know.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:56.810
Let's try a new image!

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.890
That already failed once!

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:02.600
The ghosts are the ones scaring people, not her.

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:06.940
I meant, let's try giving the ghosts a new image!

00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:09.380
Huh?

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.660
How pretty!

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:20.000
Isn't a bunch of floating fingernails still scary?

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:28.500
The classroom door will open momentarily.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:31.810
Please stand behind the white line.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:34.240
Okay!

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:37.260
The door is opening.

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:46.060
You're like a totally different person!

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:51.940
I'm, like, the gorgeous,
ill-fated ghost babe now, right?

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:54.450
As long as your mouth stays shut, yes.

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:02.680
Who's that?!

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:05.080
How d-dare you?!

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.590
You?!

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.210
Opening. Closing.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:12.720
Shake, shake.

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:15.600
O-Okay, I'm off!

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:17.720
The door is opening.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:21.350
Good luck.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:24.510
Make sure you haven't forgotten anything.

00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:26.220
The door is closing.

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:32.090
A ghost with a new image is still a ghost, isn't it?

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:33.000
Yep.

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:39.830
It still didn't work.

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:41.580
I figured.

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:46.290
We've got no other option but to ask Hanako.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:51.100
Hanako represents all the school ghosts,
so if people see that she's not scary,

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:54.550
maybe they won't be afraid of the others.

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:58.050
Huh?

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:00.640
I'm sorry! It's my fault!

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:03.640
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:17.030
Is this okay?

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:20.230
Yeah! That's really cute!

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:21.410
Wonderful.

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:23.830
Y-You think so?

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:25.590
No snarky remarks?

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:27.330
Perish the thought.

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:30.940
That ought to do it.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:31.800
Yep.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:32.720
Yeah!

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:33.460
Yes.

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:37.060
What?

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:38.710
It's true, I swear!

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:46.930
Huh?

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:48.940
Huh?

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:53.110
I really tried my best, man...

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:54.610
"Man"?

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:58.620
I'm sorry I couldn't help.

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:00.950
You're plenty cute just as you are!

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:05.090
Hey, it's Doofus Yamada.

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:06.950
What's he up to?

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:19.100
Really?

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:19.990
Yeah!

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:34.760
Time for the roll call.

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:36.790
Aizawa.

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:37.460
Here.

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:39.350
Akaishi.

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:40.090
Here.

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:41.540
Amami.

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:43.150
Amami?

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:46.370
<i>She's not paying attention.</i>

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:48.760
<i>Are they gonna answer for her again?!</i>

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:51.280
Present.

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:54.500
Greetings.

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:58.010
What the hell?!

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:02.920
You're telling me this is...

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:05.440
The roll-call samurai?

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:07.650
It looks like a normal teddy bear to me.

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:10.400
It is true!

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:12.760
How cute!

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:17.910
Apparently, the spirits are drawn to things I make.

00:11:18.330 --> 00:11:19.890
Then, you made this?

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:20.620
Hooray!

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:25.660
Yes. Ogawa invited me to the art room one day...

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:27.250
Wow.

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:29.060
Really?

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:32.000
Yeah. Amami's been down lately,

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.200
so I wanted to cheer her up.

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:36.660
Hey, you're all right, Ogawa.

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:39.260
And this...

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:43.100
is my creation!

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:45.810
Isn't he cute?

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:46.950
Well?

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:49.590
I-Is "cute" the word?

00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:53.150
<i>If not for that...</i>

00:11:55.750 --> 00:11:57.820
Why is she into that stuff, anyway?

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:59.660
Who has the guts to ask her?

00:11:59.660 --> 00:12:03.890
So, Ogawa, what is it with
you and rotting corpses?

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:04.970
He asked!

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:06.830
Only Doofus Yamada could pull that off!

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:10.340
Actually...

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:14.610
It's because of this manga.

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:17.640
A manga?

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:20.140
That copy looks really old.

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:23.380
My dad went to this high school,

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:27.900
and he happened to still have this old manga club release.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:32.310
There was a boy who was cursed with immortality.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:37.390
In order to reunite with his departed lover,

00:12:37.390 --> 00:12:38.720
he endured much persecution

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:42.410
to finally arrive at the bridge to heaven.

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:46.470
You're crying?!

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:48.120
Was there something there to cry over?!

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:50.610
Well, he...

00:12:51.260 --> 00:12:54.920
He was persecuted just for having
rotten flesh! It's not fair!

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:57.720
He had a lover, even though
his flesh was rotting away...

00:12:58.270 --> 00:13:01.180
Meanwhile, I... I...

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:07.680
<i>I guess there are all kinds of suffering.</i>

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:15.280
<i>What a beautiful story.</i>

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:18.640
<i>But in this scene...</i>

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:21.910
<i>This cat looks familiar...</i>

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:30.910
I sure am glad Ogawa's thing is
nothing like Amami's, though.

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:40.730
This presence...

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:45.760
What happened?!

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:51.600
Please, you beautiful young lady!

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:55.270
Take me to the bridge to heaven!

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:58.550
I-It's actually moving!

00:13:58.550 --> 00:14:00.190
Ogawa, are you okay?!

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:04.690
With pleasure!

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:07.650
It's hopeless! She's enamored!

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:11.670
Ogawa!

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:15.260
Did you help her make that thing, too?

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:17.050
I'm sorry...

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:19.710
But who's possessing it?

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:22.050
What if it's an evil spirit?

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:23.600
She could get in an accident...

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:27.470
Or get spirited away to another world!

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:32.720
<i>Or become one of them...</i>

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:41.040
Don't be fooled by that rotten jerk!

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:41.390
Wait for us!

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:43.360
Wait up!
Wait for us!

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:45.330
A lovers' spat?

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:49.640
Yay!

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:51.080
Hurry!

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:56.630
Hey, where's the bridge to heaven?

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:00.050
Beneath the light of the sunset, apparently.

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:01.550
What does that mean?

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:04.360
The beam of light that shines
during the witching hour.

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:06.550
They call it a bridge in here.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:07.940
Yay!

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:08.550
Sparkle!

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:15.230
That light there? We've gotta catch them!

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:17.300
So fast!

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:19.480
How incredible you are!

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:23.280
Aw, gosh!

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:30.400
She's annoyed.

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:33.050
Eye for an eye.

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:35.290
Let's have the roll-call samurai handle him!

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:38.290
Hey, maybe...

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:41.700
It'll be like something out of a fairy tale.

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:42.770
Have at thee!
It'll be like something out of a fairy tale.

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:43.300
Have at thee!

00:15:53.690 --> 00:15:57.190
Halt...

00:15:57.190 --> 00:15:58.090
We expected too much of a ghost!

00:15:58.090 --> 00:16:00.190
Halt...
We expected too much of a ghost!

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:06.360
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:08.700
<i>If he... If he were to...</i>

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:11.950
I just used this tale to my advantage!

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:14.450
<i>If something happens to Ogawa...</i>

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:16.450
<i>But then, if he really...</i>

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:20.820
I have lived the same tale. Please, help me!

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:23.790
<i>If he really needs help...</i>

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:27.090
Whee!

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:37.100
Wait!

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:39.840
The difference from one
person to the next is intense.

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:47.190
It's getting cloudy.

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:49.620
The bridge of light...

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:11.050
Will that do for a bridge of light?

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:26.360
Thank you, beautiful girl.

00:17:28.550 --> 00:17:31.200
Now I can finally go to heaven.

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:33.530
Farewell.

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:34.670
Flump.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:37.740
Stay with me.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.100
Please, don't die!

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.150
Ogawa...

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:05.220
Amami...

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:09.330
He...

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:13.150
He made it to heaven, right?

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:16.870
Yes.

00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:19.130
Definitely.

00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:23.000
This was for the best, right?

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:31.050
What are you so enamored with?

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:32.390
Huh?!

00:18:33.350 --> 00:18:35.510
How can you tell that thing not to die?!

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:37.520
He's already been dead for ages!

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:41.520
But he was cursed with immortality,
so he wasn't dead, right?

00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:43.770
You have a point.

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:48.460
This is so confusing!

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:52.610
That was ridiculous.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:54.340
Let's go home.

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:55.700
Seriously, it never ends around here.

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:56.870
Wait!
Seriously, it never ends around here.

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:57.690
Wait!

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:06.390
<i>Was the person in the doll</i>

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:09.920
<i>someone involved in the making of this book?</i>

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:16.510
<i>Who would've thought they'd
find the book from back then?</i>

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:21.140
<i>For letting me model for it,</i>

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:24.350
<i>I guess it's not so bad making
a dream or two come true—</i>

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:28.830
Good morning.

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:44.510
C-Come on, let's get to class.

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:55.080
Don't let it get you down.

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:57.740
They'll understand eventually.

00:19:57.740 --> 00:19:58.550
Right.

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:00.390
This will cheer you up.

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:02.430
Enough of that thing!

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:08.680
Don't get so upset over a bunch
of clueless underclassmen.

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:11.400
You've got...

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:15.730
M... M...

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:17.990
Inoue?

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:20.870
You've got us!

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:22.620
Yamada brought that upon himself.

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:24.070
Wh-Why?
Yamada brought that upon himself.

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:24.730
Yep.

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:29.870
Doofus Yamada, is it time yet?

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:32.580
That's right!

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:34.420
Amami, you have visitors.

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:37.770
I... do?

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:40.680
Yeah, they want to take a picture with you.

00:20:42.520 --> 00:20:44.850
Ready? Okay!

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:50.250
Weren't they scared of her?

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:53.850
Well, you know how she's been
busy with the ghosts lately?

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:56.100
Apparently, they heard about it.

00:20:56.720 --> 00:20:59.500
She's actually quite popular
with some of the girls.

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:02.620
She's the upperclassman they can
always get a ghost photo out of!

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:05.290
What is she, a ghost photo app?

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:11.710
Isn't that a win for the ghosts, not Amami?

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:14.710
Well, it's a start, right?

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:18.340
I'm so happy I got to take a picture with you!

00:21:18.740 --> 00:21:22.260
Let's help people understand
Amami more and more.

00:21:22.770 --> 00:21:24.590
Oh, over there.

00:21:25.140 --> 00:21:29.480
Yet another set of bonds
created for her by the ghosts.

00:21:31.490 --> 00:21:34.730
They might even get to be closer
friends to her than we are.

00:21:35.030 --> 00:21:37.010
That wouldn't happen!

00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:41.110
What?

00:21:41.680 --> 00:21:44.230
Would you all like to take a picture with us?

00:21:44.230 --> 00:21:45.740
No way!

00:21:48.230 --> 00:21:51.080
O-Oh, fine...

00:23:41.440 --> 00:23:43.980
It feels like we just started our second year,

00:23:43.980 --> 00:23:45.530
and summer is already here!

00:23:45.820 --> 00:23:48.080
Time sure does fly.

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:52.500
I guess I can feel that way
because my days with Inoue

00:23:52.500 --> 00:23:55.630
and all my friends are so fun and fulfilling.

00:23:55.630 --> 00:24:01.260
So, I've invited everyone to my house
to celebrate the Star Festival...

00:24:01.260 --> 00:24:05.260
Next time on Re-Kan!: "My Wish."

00:24:05.260 --> 00:24:09.250
If I could ask for one thing, I'd...
